    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "For low-stakes, high-volume applications, lean toward autonomy. Content recommendations, search result ranking, email autocomplete-these can use AI aggressively because individual errors are low-cost and users naturally learn to ignore bad suggestions. The guardrails here focus on avoiding catastrophic failures (leaking PII, generating offensive content) rather than ensuring every output is perfect. You validate for safety, not correctness. This maximizes the AI's value while keeping costs and latency low."
